{
 "section": "01",
 "slug": "01-hook",
 "heading": "## 01 — HOOK",
 "text": "How did people with no cranes, no wheels, and no steel move stones heavier than a blue whale? Some of these builders never had the wheel. Others had it, and it barely helped. A city built on the sea from columns of black rock. Three temple blocks, each heavier than a loaded jumbo jet. And giant carved pillars, raised before farming took hold. Nine structures. And the real answers are stranger than the myths.",
 "text_chars": 411,
 "previous_text": null,
 "next_text": "We're counting down from nine to one. For each site: what survives today, how it was most likely built, and what nobody knows yet.",
